course: dictionary
lesson: 7755
title: The pupa stage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A butterfly does not change into a butterfly in one step. It goes through stages, and the pupa is one of them. «A butterfly has four very different stages: egg, caterpillar (larva), chrysalis (pupa) and adult.» The pupa comes after the caterpillar and before the adult, so it must be the stage in the middle.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Inside a chrysalis the caterpillar's body breaks down and is rebuilt as a butterfly.» The insect is changing inside a case and is not crawling about, so a pupa is a resting, changing stage. The dictionary says the insect rests and changes inside a case.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Beetles have a life in four stages: egg, grub, pupa and adult.» If a pupa is the resting stage between the grub and the adult, the sentence still makes sense. Not every insect has a pupa stage, so the word says "some insects".
fact: A pupa is the stage in the life of some insects, between the larva and the adult.
fact: A butterfly pupa is called a chrysalis.
fact: A moth pupa is usually inside a cocoon.
fact: During the pupa stage the body is completely rebuilt, and this change is called metamorphosis.
fact: The plural of pupa can be pupae or pupas.
exercise: In a butterfly's life, which stage comes just before the adult? | Caterpillar | *Pupa, also called a chrysalis | Egg | Metamorphosis
exercise: What is a butterfly pupa called? | Cocoon | Larva | Egg | *Chrysalis
exercise: During the pupa stage the body is completely rebuilt. What is this big change called? | *Metamorphosis | Camouflage | Hibernation | Migration
test: Priya says a pupa is a caterpillar that eats all day. What is wrong with her idea? | It is a bird's egg | It is a very large adult butterfly | *It is a resting, changing stage inside a case, not an eating caterpillar
test: Sam finds a moth's pupa. Where is it usually found? | Inside an egg shell | Floating in the sea | Sitting bare on a leaf | *Inside a cocoon
exam: In «to get the long thread most cocoons are heated, so the pupa inside dies», what is inside the cocoon? | Silk | Water | A moth's wings | *A pupa
